{
  "id": "COMPOUND:228 - DISEASE:1010",
  "verbalization": "Nevirapine is implicated in the development of Enterocolitis, Pseudomembranous, through a multi-step mechanism involving dehydrogenase/reductase 7C. This enzyme is affected by nevirapine and is causally linked to the condition, as it contributes to the development of the syndrome. The evidence suggests that nevirapine disrupts the function of dehydrogenase/reductase 7C, which in turn leads to the formation of the condition. This pathway is supported by the observed causal relationships between nevirapine and dehydrogenase/reductase 7C, and between dehydrogenase/reductase 7C and Enterocolitis, Pseudomembranous. The presence of alternative pathways, such as the involvement of ribosomal protein L41 pseudogene 2, adds complexity to the mechanism, but the core link between nevirapine and the condition remains consistent across the evidence. The integration of these pathways highlights the role of dehydrogenase/reductase 7C as a central mediator in the pathogenesis of Enterocolitis, Pseudomembranous, under the influence of nevirapine.",
